00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:30.690
Speaker 3: He's a triune God.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:38.450
Speaker 3: Three persons, one being, Father, son, Holy Spirit, co equal, co eternal.

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:47.010
Speaker 3: All three speak as God, all three function as God, all three exist as God, and all three are worshipped as God.

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:47.690
Speaker 3: I'll take it again.

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:54.530
Speaker 3: All three speak as God, function as God, exist as God, and are worshipped as God.

00:07:55.170 --> 00:08:04.130
Speaker 3: In the Quran, God introduces himself as one person, categorically says he has no partners, he has no one.

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:10.610
Speaker 3: In fact, the God of the Bible acknowledges his Son, the Father acknowledges the Son in many places and calls him God.

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:11.500
